🎬 ARTEX — THE WORLD BUFFERING

25s | 16:9 | Mature Digital Atmosphere
No kinetic bursts. No climax.

CORE RULES

❌ No dramatic character motion
❌ No cinematic hero gestures
❌ No obvious “glitch effects” spam

✅ Continuous environmental motion
✅ Micro-camera drift
✅ Glitch is systemic, not decorative
✅ Music drives visual instability

VISUAL PRINCIPLE
The world is unstable.
They are stable.
That contrast creates tension.

AUDIO DESIGN
Tempo: 88–92 BPM
Style: Industrial ambient × lo-fi glitch
Texture layers:

• Low sub-bass pulse every 2 bars
• Metallic wind (wide stereo)
• Crackling vinyl noise
• Very faint distorted harmonic vocal layer (ghostlike, not lyrical)
• No percussion until 16s
• No drop

The track must feel like a system trying to boot.

STRUCTURE (25 seconds)
0–4s
Wide shot.
Golden embers moving normally.
Wind pushes debris across foreground.
Very subtle horizontal scanline interference, barely visible.
Camera slow 2% push-in over 4s.
The fairies remain perfectly steady.
Not frozen — but unnaturally steady.
Hair and wings move only 10% compared to debris.
Something is wrong.

4–8s
Micro pixel-shear distortion ripples through the ruins in background.
Not full-frame.
Localized, like corrupted geometry.
Ash particles slightly misalign for 3–4 frames (tiny displacement error).
Characters remain unaffected.
Sub-bass pulse slightly louder.

8–12s
Wind intensifies.
Debris moves diagonally now.
Foreground flickers brightness in sync with bass.
Very faint digital compression artifacts appear in sky gradient.
Fairies still eerily composed.
A subtle 1-degree head tilt from one — barely perceptible.
Alive, but not reacting to storm.

12–14s

Pre-glitch tension.

Metallic wind rises.
Vinyl crackle becomes clearer.

Background saturation slowly drains 10%.

Particles start jittering for micro-frames.

🔥 KEY MOMENT — 14s to 15s

Entire background desaturates to grayscale.

The ruins.
The sky.
The ash.

Only the two figures remain gold.
No camera movement.
Wind continues moving debris.
This lasts exactly 1 second.
Audio drops into low filtered hum.

15–18s

Snap back to full color.
Not smoothly — sharp digital correction.
A brief horizontal frame tear at the horizon.
Sub-bass returns stronger.
Scanline interference more visible now.

18–22s

Reality destabilizes subtly.
Background geometry flickers 2–3 pixels left-right for a frame.
Particles occasionally freeze for a single frame before resuming.
The fairies remain anchored.
Camera push-in ends.
They are closer now.

22–25s

System stabilizing.
Glitch artifacts reduce.
Wind softens slightly.
Vinyl crackle remains.
For the final 2 seconds:
A faint golden halo pulses once around them —
not magical —
like a rendering selection highlight.
Cut to black on unresolved low tone.

No fade.